<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Danubyu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1825</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-burmese-war">First Anglo-Burmese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Danubyu was fought in March and April 1825 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-burmese-war">First Anglo-Burmese War</a>, when a British force attacked the Burmese fortified position at Danubyu in the Irrawaddy delta. The Burmese commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maha-bandula">Maha Bandula</a> was killed by a mortar shell on 1 April 1825, and his army abandoned the stockade, opening the way for the British advance up the Irrawaddy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-danubyu.jpg" alt="Battle of Danubyu" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Print made by: Henry Pyall After: Thomas Stothard After: Capt Thornton Published by: Thomas Clay · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Combined_Forces_under_Brig._Cotton,_C.B._and_Captains_Alexander,_C.B._%26_Chads,_R.N._passing_the_Fortress_of_Donabue_to_effect_a_junction_with_Sir_Archibald_Campbell,_on_the_27th_March_1825_1241485001_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
